	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Paintless dent repair FAQ</h2>
			<div class="faq-list">
				<details class="faq-item">
					<summary>What is paintless dent repair?</summary>
					<p>Paintless dent repair (PDR) is a technique that removes dents from vehicle panels without sanding, filling, or repainting. A technician uses specialized tools to reshape the metal from behind the panel, preserving your factory paint finish.</p>
				</details>
				<details class="faq-item">
					<summary>How much does paintless dent repair cost near Cleveland, Ohio?</summary>
					<p>PDR cost depends on dent size, location, and accessibility. Small door dings typically range from $75–$150. Hail damage is quoted per panel after an inspection so we can price the repair accurately.</p>
				</details>
				<details class="faq-item">
					<summary>Where does All Dent PDR provide service?</summary>
					<p>All Dent PDR operates a shop at 7695 Granger Rd, Cleveland, OH 44125, serving Greater Cleveland and all of Northeast Ohio with paintless dent repair, hail damage repair, and door ding removal.</p>
				</details>
				<details class="faq-item">
					<summary>How long does a typical PDR repair take?</summary>
					<p>Most single-dent repairs are completed in 1–3 hours. Multi-panel hail damage may take a full day. We provide a timeline upfront so you can plan accordingly.</p>
				</details>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
